    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Alert rules and what to do",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "| Alert | Fires when | What to do |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Late-event rate above 5% (5 min)** | late events / events over the last 5 minutes is above 5% and there are at least 20 events | Check the simulator for clock skew or replayed old events, then the Silver watermark. Live runs only: history mode is all late by rule. |\n| **Quarantine share above 2% (5 min)** | quarantined / (events + quarantined) over 5 minutes is above 2% (at least 20 rows) | Group `silver_quarantine` by reason for the last 10 minutes and fix the producer that sends the bad rows. |\n| **Silver job silent for 2 minutes** | the Silver job heartbeat is older than 2 minutes (no data also fires) | Check docker compose ps and the fs-pipeline logs; restart the Silver job with the same command and checkpoints and confirm the heartbeat age drops under 30 s. |\n| **No events for 5 minutes** | no Silver event arrived in the last 5 minutes (no data also fires) | Check that the simulator and the Silver job run; restart the Silver job and confirm the event line recovers. |\n\nNotifications go to the `fs-webhook` contact point (`scripts/alert_sink.py`, port 9099)."
      }
    }
  ]
